  "decision": "rejected",
  "reason": "Effect did not replicate at scale. Stage-by-stage: screening 101-99 (50.5%), main 169-131 (56.3%, p=0.028), confirmation 264-236 (52.8%), extension 491-509 (49.1%). POOLED 2000 games: 1025-975 (51.25%), CI [49.06, 53.44], z=1.118, p=0.264. Zero draws, timeouts, illegal actions or crashes across all 2020 games. IMPORTANT METHODOLOGICAL RESULT: at n=1000 this stood at 53.4% with p=0.0315 -- nominally significant, CI excluding 50% -- and 1000 further games on a fresh seed pulled it to 51.25% with the interval spanning 50. The apparent significance was a multiple-looks artifact: screening, main, confirmation and an extension are four opportunities for noise to cross a threshold, and one of them did. The pre-committed 55% effect-size bar is what prevented adoption at the n=1000 look; a p-value gate alone would have accepted this. The mechanism is not harmful and may be very slightly positive, but it is not distinguishable from zero and does not justify promotion. Operator's conditional formulation was still materially better than the blanket EXP-0007 reorder (45.0%), so the domain insight was sound; the remaining effect is just too small to bank.",
